# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working tree on every OS.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true, every source file gets
# CRLF, and `biome check src/` reports a formatting diff on all 85 files — the Windows CI
# job added for issue #69 failed exactly this way, and any Windows contributor would hit
# the same wall running lint locally. `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is what pins the
# working-tree ending regardless of the user's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
